From: WikiReader Linux port
Subject: [PATCH] binfmt_elf_fdpic: check the logical core stream position

Pipes do not advance file->f_pos, so a successful piped FDPIC core dump
always triggers the final size warning. The coredump helpers already
track the stream position independently of the output file. Include
any pending skip, which is also part of the logical position.

diff --git a/fs/binfmt_elf_fdpic.c b/fs/binfmt_elf_fdpic.c
--- a/fs/binfmt_elf_fdpic.c
+++ b/fs/binfmt_elf_fdpic.c
@@ -1648,11 +1648,11 @@ static int elf_fdpic_core_dump(struct coredump_params *cprm)
 			goto end_coredump;
 	}
 
-	if (cprm->file->f_pos != offset) {
+	if (cprm->pos + cprm->to_skip != offset) {
 		/* Sanity check */
 		printk(KERN_WARNING
-		       "elf_core_dump: file->f_pos (%lld) != offset (%lld)\n",
-		       cprm->file->f_pos, offset);
+		       "elf_core_dump: position (%lld) != offset (%lld)\n",
+		       cprm->pos + cprm->to_skip, offset);
 	}
 
 end_coredump:
